From 990c761ef82bab4babc5e9f509258a7edb7822e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:54:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 34/63] glm cuda: two ranks on one host gather a window's
 partials by peer stores, not NCCL

At TP=2 on one host, every all-gather on the engine stream of at most 512 KiB a rank (a decode or verify window's
fp32 partials, up to 32 shared rows; the drafter's partials and top lists; the greedy pick's pairs) goes through
tp_group's new p2p hook instead of ncclAllGather. Each rank's tf_glm_p2p_gather blocks store its share into the
peer's inbox (CUDA IPC, mapped at startup), release a flag line there, acquire their own, and copy the peer's share
into the gathered buffer. The gathered buffer holds the same bytes in the same slots, and hcPost sums them in rank
order as before, so the bits are unchanged. Two parities keep consecutive epochs apart (the host's
epoch counter skips 0, the flags' initial value, by wrapping to 2, so the parities alternate across the wrap too); a
wait past TF_GLM_P2P_GATHER_TIMEOUT_S (60) or an aborted group writes a status word that Group.check raises.

Both ranks always meet in the setup exchange; a rank that wants it off (TF_GLM_P2P_GATHER=0) or cannot map the
other's memory leaves both on NCCL. Larger gathers and other streams' stay on NCCL. TF_GLM_P2P_GATHER_MAX_KB caps it.

Measured on 2x RTX PRO 6000 (PCIe Gen5 x8 each, PHB): 16 KiB a rank 3.2-3.6 us a launched call against
ncclAllGather's 10.3 us; in a 90-site decode-shaped chain 3.3 against 6.1 us exposed at one row, 8.4 against 16.9
at eight. Kernel check (3000 mixed-size calls, 16 B to 512 KiB): no mismatch.

